# 13. COGNITIVE PERFORMANCE ANALYTICS

At the end of the session, calculate the following metrics.

### A. Target fixation percentage

Percentage of valid session time spent within the primary target area.

Formula:

Time within primary target / Total valid observation time × 100.

### B. Distractor capture count

Number of distinct times the participant's simulated gaze enters a distraction area.

### C. Average distraction duration

Average time spent in a distraction area per distinct distraction event.

### D. Refocusing latency

Time between leaving the primary target and returning to it.

Report the average and, where possible, median.

### E. Sustained attention consistency

Compare performance across the early and later portions of the session.

### F. Response accuracy

Correct target responses divided by total valid target opportunities.

### G. Reaction-time variability

Calculate the standard deviation of valid reaction times.

### H. Stage-by-stage performance

Compare the metrics from each stage to identify how performance changed as cognitive demands increased.

Important:

Do not use arbitrary thresholds to classify participants as ADHD-positive or ADHD-negative.

Do not produce a diagnostic probability.

Do not label a participant as having impaired attention based on a single session.

All scores should be presented as descriptive experimental performance indicators.

